@namespace FormCraft.ForFluentUI

@* Help text is rendered here, by the container, rather than bound to each input's own `Message`
   parameter.

   `Message` looked like the natural slot - Fluent documents it as "the message to display below the
   field" - but it is owned by the input's validation display: measured on v5 RC5, FluentTextInput
   and FluentNumberInput overwrite a caller-supplied Message with their own validation string
   ("This field is required"), while FluentCheckbox, FluentDatePicker and FluentSelect leave it
   alone. Binding it would give help text that appears on three field types and silently vanishes on
   the other two - which is worse than a uniform mechanism, because the gap is invisible until a
   user needs the instruction.

   Per-field instructions are the WCAG 2.1 3.3.2 mechanism this adapter otherwise honours through
   `aria-required`, so it gets a slot the adapter controls. `aria-describedby` wires it to the input
   for assistive technology. *@
@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Text))
{
    <div id="@Id" class="formcraft-field-help">@Text</div>
}
